*** CarbonLEI Maude checks: one command per line, each run in its own Maude process by run.sh.
*** Each line is "<expected> : <command>": none = no solution, found = a solution, true = the LTL
*** formula holds, counterexample = it does not. run.sh fails if any result differs. Results: README.md.
select CARBONLEI .
*** --- A. Safety: every property expected to hold (safetyBad, twelve properties), expected: No solution
none : search keriInst(up, 4) =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
none : search (keriInst(up, 4) withDelta 2) =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
none : search suspInst(3) =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
none : search (suspInst(3) withDelta 2) =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
none : search revInst(4) =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
none : search dupInst(4) =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
*** Two of the twelve also searched on their own, on the instances where they can be exercised:
*** registration during suspension is rejected (regSuspendedBad); no revision by another body while
*** the issuer is active (notReportIssuerBad, NotReportIssuer). Non-vacuity: regAfterLift, revWitness (B)
none : search suspInst(3) =>* { S:Conf } such that regSuspendedBad(S:Conf) .
none : search revInst(4) =>* { S:Conf } such that regSuspendedBad(S:Conf) .
none : search revInst(4) =>* { S:Conf } such that notReportIssuerBad(S:Conf) .
*** --- B. Non-vacuity: the safe instances do reach the interesting states, expected: a solution
found : search [1] revInst(4) =>* { S:Conf } such that revWitness(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) =>* { S:Conf } such that contestedAfterKeri(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) =>* { S:Conf } such that twoImporters(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) =>* { S:Conf } such that regAfterLift(S:Conf) .
*** --- C. Sanity counterexample: the watcher stopped (down) or later than delta (late), expected: a solution (keriBad)
found : search [1] keriInst(down, 4) =>* { S:Conf } such that keriBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(late, 4) =>* { S:Conf } such that keriBad(S:Conf) .
*** --- D. Documented limits, expected: a solution each (T2/T18 sync window, T19 (8), CR6, attack 4 on-chain)
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) =>* { S:Conf } such that keriRace(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] dupInst(4) =>* { S:Conf } such that onchainSumBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) =>* { S:Conf } such that viewsBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) =>* { S:Conf } such that impostorRegistered(S:Conf) .
*** --- E. Mutants: 17 mutants, each removing or weakening one guard or check, 32 runs; expected: a solution each
*** contract, claim and ledger guards
found : search [1] dupInst(4) +mut noClaimCap =>* { S:Conf } such that p1Bad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut noOverClaimed =>* { S:Conf } such that p1Bad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] dupInst(4) +mut noCovered =>* { S:Conf } such that ledgerBad(S:Conf) .
*** contract, registration guards (noSuspGuard and noIssuerGuard from our own red-team review)
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut noAuthGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that regAfterRevBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut noSuspGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that regInactiveBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut noSuspGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that authBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut noSuspGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that regInactiveBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut noSuspGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut noExpiryGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that regInactiveBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut noIssuerGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that notReportIssuerBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut noIssuerGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
*** contract, for the two explicit properties (added 11 October): the suspension test off by one
*** tick, and the issuer test ignoring a lift
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut noSuspGuard =>* { S:Conf } such that regSuspendedBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut suspSameTick =>* { S:Conf } such that regSuspendedBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut suspSameTick =>* { S:Conf } such that regSuspendedBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut issuerIgnoresLift =>* { S:Conf } such that notReportIssuerBad(S:Conf) .
*** verifier checks
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut noCheck5 =>* { S:Conf } such that replayBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut noCheck5 =>* { S:Conf } such that ledgerBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut noRoot =>* { S:Conf } such that authBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] dupInst(4) +mut noScope =>* { S:Conf } such that ledgerBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut noContested =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut noContested =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut noContested =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut winLeftOpen =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut winLeftOpen =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut winLeftOpen =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut winRightOpen =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut winRightOpen =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut winRightOpen =>* { S:Conf } such that windowBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut winRightOpen =>* { S:Conf } such that keriBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] suspInst(3) +mut winRightOpen =>* { S:Conf } such that safetyBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] keriInst(up, 4) +mut noEvidenceRev =>* { S:Conf } such that evidenceBad(S:Conf) .
found : search [1] revInst(4) +mut noSupersede =>* { S:Conf } such that supersededBad(S:Conf) .
select CARBONLEI-LTL .
*** --- F. LTL. Evidence: eventual sync with the watcher up (true) and down (counterexample). The rest
*** are SANITY CHECKS, NOT SECURITY CLAIMS: they hold by construction of the model (no rule removes a
*** revocation or a suspension, and registeredAt never changes) and are not evidence about the code:
*** eventual sync with the watcher late (true: the formula does not check the bound delta), CONTESTED
*** never VALID again (sanity), P6 (sanity), and [] safeP (the same as the searches of A).
true : red modelCheck(keriInst(up, 3), [] (keriRevokedP(a1) -> <> chainRevokedP(a1))) .
counterexample : red modelCheck(keriInst(down, 3), [] (keriRevokedP(a1) -> <> chainRevokedP(a1))) .
true : red modelCheck(keriInst(late, 3), [] (keriRevokedP(a1) -> <> chainRevokedP(a1))) .
true : red modelCheck(keriInst(up, 3), [] (contestedP(r1) -> [] ~ validP(r1))) .
true : red modelCheck(suspInst(2), [] (contestedP(r1) -> [] ~ validP(r1))) .
true : red modelCheck(keriInst(up, 3), [] (chainRevokedP(a1) -> [] chainRevokedP(a1))) .
true : red modelCheck(keriInst(up, 3), [] safeP) .
true : red modelCheck(revInst(3), [] safeP) .
*** --- G. CR1: owner-key compromise, rotation and revocation (module CARBONLEI-CR1, a separate model;
*** cr1Inst(contract, body monitoring, watcher monitoring of rotations, watcher monitoring of WATCHER
*** grants, owner key may drop the watcher, last tick)). Since 14 October the attacker may also
*** propose WATCHER_ROLE for an account of its own (two-step, ROTATION_DELAY, cancellable by a current
*** watcher), suspend and lift with it, and a suspended body cannot cancel a rotation (M2). Ticks
*** 0..10 (the attack below needs 9 when the body cancels at once). One property, cr1Bad: no report
*** is revoked by an address its body did not control.
select CARBONLEI-CR1 .
*** V1 (deployed): rotation and revocation in one block, even with all monitors; expected: a solution
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v1, bWatch, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
*** V2 under a monitoring assumption, the watcher keeping its role; expected: No solution. (1) the
*** body or the watcher cancels each rotation proposal within ROTATION_DELAY (the watcher need not
*** cancel WATCHER grants); (2) the body misses the rotation, and the watcher suspends the body within
*** REVOKE_HOLD of the rotation and cancels every WATCHER grant to another account within its delay
none : search cr1Inst(v2, bWatch, wNone, gNone, false, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
none : search cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
*** Finding of 14 October (No solution while the model left role grants out): once the owner key has
*** dropped the watcher, the body's own cancellation is not enough. The key grants WATCHER to an
*** account of its own (nobody is left to cancel), suspends the body (a suspended body cannot cancel,
*** M2), lets the rotation execute, lifts the suspension and revokes; expected: a solution each, the
*** second on a path where the honest watcher never suspended (cr1BadThiefSusp)
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bWatch, wNone, gNone, true, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bWatch, wNone, gNone, true, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1BadThiefSusp(S:CrConf) .
*** V2 without monitoring: the attack completes (a solution), but not before tick 6 = 144 h (No
*** solution; searched to tick 7, which contains every path to a revocation before tick 6, at a
*** quarter of the states of tick 10)
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wNone, gNone, true, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
none : search cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wNone, gNone, true, 7) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1BadBefore(6, S:CrConf) .
*** V2, weaker monitoring; expected: a solution each. A watcher that reacts only to RevocationQueued;
*** a watcher whose role the owner key removes first; a watcher that suspends after the rotation but
*** does not cancel the attacker's WATCHER grant (the grant's account lifts the suspension and the
*** revocation executes in the same block)
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnQueued, gCancel, false, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, true, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gNone, false, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
*** Non-vacuity of the two V2 No-solution results; expected: a solution each. A rotation proposal
*** cancelled and time at the bound; the rotation done, a revocation queued, the body suspended and
*** time at the bound; a WATCHER grant to the attacker cancelled and time at the bound
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bWatch, wNone, gNone, false, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that cancelWitness(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that suspendWitness(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) =>* { S:CrConf } such that grantCancelWitness(S:CrConf) .
*** V2 mutants (5 mutants, 5 runs), on the instance of result (2); expected: a solution each.
*** REVOKE_HOLD removed; executeRevocation without the requester check; WATCHER granted at once
*** (no RoleGrantNeedsDelay, H2); cancelRoleGrant not open to the watcher; liftSuspension open to the
*** owner without WATCHER_ROLE
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) +mut noHold =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) +mut noLapse =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) +mut grantNow =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) +mut noGrantCancel =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
found : search [1] cr1Inst(v2, bNone, wOnRotation, gCancel, false, 10) +mut liftByOwner =>* { S:CrConf } such that cr1Bad(S:CrConf) .
